# Theme switching is a menu action with no terminal to carry a password prompt,
# and it repaints the boot splash and login screen on every switch, so this one
# write must not stop for a password. Each argument is spelled out as six hex
# digits rather than a wildcard: the grant covers four colors and nothing else,
# and sudoers matches a command's arguments exactly, so it cannot be stretched
# into extra ones. The writer revalidates the same shape, since the terminal
# path does not come through this rule.
%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/omarchy-theme-set-login-colors [0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f] [0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f] [0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f] [0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]
